  "question": {
    "text": "$A B$ is a vertical pole with $B$ at the ground level and $A$ at the top. $A$ man finds that the angle of elevation of the point $A$ from a certain point $C$ on the ground is $60^{\\circ}$. He moves away from the pole along the line $B C$ to a point $D$ such that $C D=7 \\mathrm{~m}$. From $D$ the angle of elevation of the point $A$ is $45^{\\circ}$. Then the height of the pole is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "l9X76",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}-1} m$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Y3Rz7",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot(\\sqrt{3}+1) m$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9TXWi",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot(\\sqrt{3}-1) \\mathrm{m}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OE0Xr",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{BD}=\\mathrm{AB}=7+x \\\\\n& \\text { Also } \\mathrm{AB}=\\mathrm{x} \\tan 60^{\\circ}=x \\sqrt{3} \\\\\n& \\therefore x \\sqrt{3}=7+x \\\\\n& \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{3}-1} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{AB}=\\frac{7 \\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\sqrt{3}+1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2eZQMvQK9Rj8zI5Pscu4Ptwilm04Oay1aAnc1v0TI1Y.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
